# <NAME> — LLM wiki

<one sentence: what this wiki is about, and what it is deliberately NOT about>

## Layers

- `raw/` — source documents. Articles, papers, specs, notes, data files.
  Immutable: you read from them and never modify them. One file per source,
  `YYYY-MM-DD-slug.md`, with its origin URL or citation on the first line. A
  source may be renamed and given that header on first ingest, never after.
- `wiki/` — you own this entirely. Add, revise, restructure, and retire pages
  as understanding improves.
- this file — the conventions below. The only operating contract.

## Rules

1. Every claim in `wiki/` carries a citation: `(raw/<file>)` or a URL. No
   citation, no claim.
2. Separate verified from inferred. Label anything unconfirmed and say what
   would confirm it.
3. Conflicting sources: show both with citations. Never silently pick one.
4. Every page except `index.md` and `log.md` carries the frontmatter below and
   appears in `wiki/index.md`.
5. Links are `[[wikilinks]]` — Obsidian resolves them by filename, so never
   write a path, and every filename must be unique across the wiki. Link
   generously; the links are the graph.
6. One ingest updates the new page(s), every existing page the source touches,
   `index.md`, `log.md`, and `overview.md` if the big picture moved — in ONE
   commit.
7. A search hit is a lead, not evidence. Read the whole page before using
   anything from it, and cite the page rather than the hit.
8. Local-first. Never push or send anything outward without being asked.

## Pages

    wiki/index.md            catalog of every page. Read this first.
    wiki/log.md              append-only history of every operation
    wiki/overview.md         the whole wiki in a few paragraphs
    wiki/sources/<slug>.md   one per ingested source: key claims, exact quotes
    wiki/entities/<name>.md  person, company, product, project, tool
    wiki/concepts/<name>.md  a single idea, held steady
    wiki/comparisons/<a>-vs-<b>.md
    wiki/synthesis/<topic>.md   conclusions drawn across several pages

A page opens with one paragraph stating its claim, then the detail with
every factual line cited, then a `## Related` list of wikilinks.

## Frontmatter

    ---
    title: <Page Title>
    type: source | entity | concept | comparison | synthesis | overview
    created: YYYY-MM-DD
    updated: YYYY-MM-DD
    sources: [<source-filename.md>]   # filenames only, never paths
    support: solid | thin | one-source | disputed | unsupported
    verified-at: <version or tag, if this describes something versioned>
    tags: [<tag>, <tag>]
    ---

## Conventions

- Filenames: lowercase, hyphens, no spaces. Dates: `YYYY-MM-DD`.
- `log.md` newest first: `## YYYY-MM-DD · <op> — <subject>`, then `created:` /
  `updated:` / `left open:` bullets. `left open:` is mandatory; write
  `nothing` if there is nothing.
- Cite versioned material by pin — `(<repo>@<tag>:<path>:<line>)` — never by
  copying it in. A pin stays true; a copy goes stale on the next commit.
- When uncertain, write the uncertainty down rather than omitting it.
